cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use DPCexplorer, please cite the SOFTWARE by default, using the
  Zenodo concept DOI below (10.5281/zenodo.20575268), which always resolves
  to the latest release. For the methodology and full documentation, see the
  MDMC thesis (10.5281/zenodo.20847161); for a concise overview, see the
  eScience 2026 preprint (10.5281/zenodo.20766432). All related works are listed
  under "references".

type: software

title: >-
  DPCexplorer: A Django Web Application for Interactive Exploration
  of DPCfam and DPCstruct Protein Domain Classifications

version: "v1.1.0"

date-released: "2026-08-03"

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20575268"

abstract: >-

  DPCexplorer is an open-source Django 6.0.1 web application that provides
  interactive browser-based access to two large, unsupervised protein domain
  family classifications: DPCfam (81,384 sequence-based metaclusters derived
  from UniRef50 via BLASTp and Density Peak Clustering) and DPCstruct (28,246
  structure-based metaclusters derived from the AlphaFold Database via Foldseek
  and Density Peak Clustering). Raw archives were preprocessed on the ORFEO HPC
  cluster and loaded into a PostgreSQL 16.11 database optimized with B-Tree, GIN
  trigram, and functional indexes for fast lookup across millions of protein
  assignments. Built on the Model-View-Template pattern, the platform supports
  four query types (DPCfam MCID, DPCstruct MCID, Pfam ID, UniProt accession),
  serves downloadable biological files (FASTA, MSA, HMM, PDB), renders a 
  per-protein domain-architecture diagram, and embeds an interactive 3D molecular
  viewer powered by PDBe-Molstar for DPCstruct metaclusters. The platform is
  designed in alignment with FAIR Principles for Research Software (FAIR4RS)
  and is fully reproducible from the associated GitHub repository and Zenodo 
  data deposit (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20159208).


license: MIT

url: "https://dpcexplorer.areasciencepark.it"

repository-code: "https://github.com/RitAreaSciencePark/dpc_fam_and_struct_webapp"

keywords:
  - protein domain classification
  - Density Peak Clustering
  - DPCfam
  - DPCstruct
  - metacluster
  - UniRef50
  - AlphaFold2
  - Pfam
  - Django
  - PostgreSQL
  - bioinformatics
  - FAIR data
  - Mol*
  - DPCexplorer
  - web application

